+def _binding_rows_per_band(spec: dict, group_rows_for) -> dict[tuple[int, int], int]:
+    """Row-count overrides that make a binding-fed report elastic.
+
+    For every data group the spec binds:
+
+    * a band whose recovered rows all sit **past** the supplied data collapses to
+      zero rows (an empty / omitted section, or a page beyond a short table, so
+      no orphan ruled body is drawn);
+    * the band that reaches **furthest** into the group (its tail) grows to
+      absorb any rows beyond what the reference reached (longer data).
+
+    Bands fed exactly their reference rows get no override, so the 19 reference
+    reports — whose data length matches what their bands were recovered to
+    consume — stay byte-for-byte inert. A band's own ``group_offset`` /
+    ``row_data_index`` is respected, so a table the reference continues across
+    pages keeps each page's slice unchanged.
